= Labour Isn't Working

Saatchi & Saatchi bring in a poster: a long, snaking dole queue under the slogan "Labour Isn't Working. Britain's Better Off With The Conservatives."

The queue is actually Young Conservatives from Hendon, photographed again and again. It will only go up on a few dozen sites, but if Labour complains it could be front-page news.

- @run: Run it.
- @shelve: Too risky. Shelve it.

@run
on-arrival: labour_credibility -= 5; de_con += 2*(1-dissent); c2_con += 2*(1-dissent); thatcher_rating += 1; callaghan_rating -= 1; economic_liberalism -= 1
achievement: labour_isnt_working

Denis Healey denounces the poster in the Commons, and every newspaper and news bulletin reproduces it. A few thousand pounds of billboard space turns into millions of pounds' worth of free publicity.

@shelve
on-arrival: wet_dissent -= 1

The poster goes into a drawer at Charlotte Street. Maurice Saatchi is too polite to say what he thinks.
